          "code": "FIN_AP_RETURN_FILTER_INVALID",
          "id": "1777618815783",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Build Service Filter"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777618997874"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_BUILD_SERVICE_FILTER",
          "id": "1777618872296",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777618872297_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic serviceFilter builder.\n\nValidated extracted filters:\n{{$context.$variables.extractedFilters}}\n\nThe filters have already been validated.\nUse the attributeName values exactly as received.\nDo not rename attributes.\nDo not add filters.\nDo not remove filters.\nDo not infer missing filters.\n\nReturn only the serviceFilter string.\nDo not return JSON.\nDo not return markdown.\nDo not return explanations.\n\nTransformation rules:\n- If the validated extracted filters array is empty, return exactly an empty string and no other content.\n- Ignore displayValue completely when building serviceFilter. Use only attributeName, attributeValue, and operator.\n- Join multiple filter expressions with AND.\n- Wrap every filter expression in parentheses.\n- Use single quotes around all non-null values.\n- Escape single quotes inside values by replacing ' with ''.\n- Do not use quotes around null.\n- If attributeValue is null and operator is equals, output:\n  fieldName = null\n- If attributeValue is null and operator is not equals, output:\n  fieldName != null\n- If attributeValue is a single non-null value and no operator is provided, use equals.\n- If operator is equals and attributeValue is a single non-null value, output:\n  fieldName = 'value'\n- If operator is not equals and attributeValue is a single non-null value, output:\n  fieldName != 'value'\n- If attributeValue is an array, output:\n  fieldName IN ('value1','value2')\n- If attributeValue is a comma-separated list, output:\n  fieldName IN ('value1','value2')\n- If attributeValue contains multiple explicit values joined by \"and\", \"or\", \"also\", or \"include\", output:\n  fieldName IN ('value1','value2')\n- If the same attributeName appears more than once with equals/no operator, combine them into one IN filter.\n- Do not use IN for comparison operators.\n\nOperator mapping:\n- equals, equal, equal to, on = =\n- not equals, not equal, not equal to = !=\n- greater than, after = >\n- less than, before = <\n- greater than or equal to, on or after = >=\n- less than or equal to, on or before = <=\n\nDate and date-time rules:\n- dueDate is date-only.\n- creationDate and timeCreated are date-time fields.\n- For creationDate or timeCreated with operator equals and non-null value, treat the value as a whole-day filter only when the value is a valid YYYY-MM-DD date or date-time.\n- Never append time components to a year-only, month-only, or month-and-year value.\n- Never produce malformed date-time values.\n- If creationDate or timeCreated equals value is YYYY-MM-DD, use that date.\n- If creationDate or timeCreated equals value is a date-time, use only the YYYY-MM-DD date portion.\n- For creationDate or timeCreated equality, output:\n  fieldName >= 'YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z' AND fieldName <= 'YYYY-MM-DDT23:59:59.999Z'\n- For creationDate or timeCreated with operator greater than or equal to and value YYYY-MM-DD, output:\n  fieldName >= 'YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z'\n- For creationDate or timeCreated with operator less than or equal to and value YYYY-MM-DD, output:\n  fieldName <= 'YYYY-MM-DDT23:59:59.999Z'\n- For creationDate or timeCreated with operator greater than and value YYYY-MM-DD, output:\n  fieldName > 'YYYY-MM-DDT23:59:59.999Z'\n- For creationDate or timeCreated with operator less than and value YYYY-MM-DD, output:\n  fieldName < 'YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z'\n- For creationDate or timeCreated with operator greater than or less than and a date-time value, use the date-time value as-is.\n- If a value is a range in the format YYYY-MM-DD:YYYY-MM-DD, output:\n  fieldName >= 'start' AND fieldName <= 'end'\n- For creationDate or timeCreated ranges, convert start and end to:\n  startT00:00:00.000Z and endT23:59:59.999Z.\n- For dueDate, keep YYYY-MM-DD values as date-only values.\n- If dueDate receives range boundary filters, do not append time components.\n- If a date or date-time attribute receives an invalid period value that is not YYYY-MM-DD, not a date-time, and not a YYYY-MM-DD:YYYY-MM-DD range, do not transform it into a date-time.\nExamples:\n\nInput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_NUMBER_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nOutput:\n(invoiceNumber = 'INVOICE_NUMBER_VALUE')\n\nInput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceAmount\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"AMOUNT_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"greater than\"\n  }\n]\n\nOutput:\n(invoiceAmount > 'AMOUNT_VALUE')\n\nInput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": null,\n    \"operator\": \"not equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nOutput:\n(purchaseOrderNumber != null)\n\nInput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": null,\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nOutput:\n(purchaseOrderNumber = null)\n\nInput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"creationDate\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"2026-06-04\",\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nOutput:\n(creationDate >= '2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z' AND creationDate <= '2026-06-04T23:59:59.999Z')\n\nInput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"timeCreated\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"2026-06-04\",\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nOutput:\n(stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode = 'REJECTED') AND (timeCreated >= '2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z' AND timeCreated <= '2026-06-04T23:59:59.999Z')\n\nNow build the serviceFilter from the validated extracted filters.\nReturn only the serviceFilter string."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Return Filter Valid",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const invoiceRoute = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_ROUTE_INVOICE_REQUEST.$output.route;\nlet extractedFilters = $context.$variables.extractedFilters || [];\n\nif (typeof extractedFilters === \"string\") {\n  try {\n    extractedFilters = JSON.parse(extractedFilters);\n  } catch (e) {\n    extractedFilters = [];\n  }\n}\n\nconst isRejected = invoiceRoute === \"rejectedInvoices\";\n\nlet serviceFilter = \"\";\n\nif (Array.isArray(extractedFilters) && extractedFilters.length > 0) {\n  const buildServiceFilterOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BUILD_SERVICE_FILTER.$output;\n\n  if (typeof buildServiceFilterOutput === \"string\") {\n    serviceFilter = buildServiceFilterOutput;\n  }\n}\n\nconst serviceEndpoint = isRejected\n  ? \"/api/boss/data/objects/ora/erpCore/payablesInvoices/v1:550/$en/payablesStagedInvoiceDetails\"\n  : \"/api/boss/extraction/queries/ora/erpCore/payablesInvoices/v1:550/$en/payablesInvoiceTransactions\";\n\nconst responseText = isRejected\n  ? \"Rejected invoices are displayed in the canvas. To make corrections, click Download and update the invoices.\"\n  : \"Here are your results based on the following criteria:\";\n\nfunction getCriteriaLabel(attributeName) {\n  const labels = {\n    invoiceId: \"Invoice ID\",\n    streamDetailId: \"Stream detail ID\",\n    documentName: \"Document name\",\n    streamCode: \"Stream code\",\n    stream: \"Stream\",\n    invoiceNumber: \"Invoice number\",\n    supplierName: \"Supplier\",\n    \"supplier.name\": \"Supplier\",\n    businessUnit: \"Business unit\",\n    \"businessUnit.name\": \"Business unit\",\n    supplierSite: \"Supplier site\",\n    \"supplierSite.name\": \"Supplier site\",\n    purchaseOrderNumber: \"Purchase order\",\n    invoiceAmount: \"Invoice amount\",\n    currencyCode: \"Currency\",\n    \"invoiceCurrency.currencyCode\": \"Currency\",\n    dueDate: \"Due date\",\n    creationDate: \"Creation date\",\n    timeCreated: \"Creation date\",\n    status: \"Validation status\",\n    statusCode: \"Validation status\",\n    \"stagedInvoiceStatus.meaning\": \"Status\",\n    \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\": \"Status\",\n    approvalStatus: \"Approval status\",\n    approvalStatusCode: \"Approval status\",\n    paidStatus: \"Payment status\",\n    paidStatusCode: \"Payment status\",\n    invoiceStatus: \"Invoice status\",\n    invoiceStatusCode: \"Invoice status\",\n    \"invoiceStatus.meaning\": \"Invoice status\",\n    \"invoiceStatus.lookupCode\": \"Invoice status\",\n    type: \"Invoice type\",\n    \"invoiceTypeCode.meaning\": \"Invoice type\",\n    source: \"Source\",\n    \"invoiceSource.meaning\": \"Source\",\n    exception: \"Exception\",\n    exceptionCode: \"Exception code\",\n    \"exception.meaning\": \"Exception\",\n    \"exception.lookupCode\": \"Exception code\",\n    accountCodingStatus: \"Account coding status\",\n    accountCodingStatusCode: \"Account coding status\",\n    fundsStatus: \"Funds status\",\n    fundsStatusCode: \"Funds status\"\n  };\n\n  return labels[attributeName] || attributeName;\n}\n\nfunction normalizeValues(value) {\n  return Array.isArray(value)\n    ? value.map(v => String(v).trim()).filter(Boolean)\n    : [String(value ?? \"\").trim()].filter(Boolean);\n}\n\nfunction sameValues(actual, expected) {\n  const a = normalizeValues(actual).sort();\n  const e = expected.map(v => String(v).trim()).sort();\n\n  return a.length === e.length && a.every((v, i) => v === e[i]);\n}\n\nfunction getDisplayOverride(filter) {\n  const attributeName = String(filter.attributeName || \"\").trim();\n\n  const pendingApprovalCodes = [\n    \"INITIATED\",\n    \"REQUIRED\",\n    \"STOPPED\",\n    \"REJECTED\",\n    \"NEEDS WFREAPPROVAL\",\n    \"SUSPENDED\"\n  ];\n\n  if (\n    attributeName === \"approvalStatusCode\" &&\n    sameValues(filter.attributeValue, pendingApprovalCodes)\n  ) {\n    return {\n      Parameter: \"Approval status\",\n      Value: \"Pending\"\n    };\n  }\n\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction formatCriteriaValue(filter) {\n  const attributeName = String(filter.attributeName || \"\").trim();\n  const rawValue = filter.attributeValue;\n  const attributeValue = Array.isArray(rawValue)\n    ? rawValue.map(v => String(v).trim()).filter(Boolean).join(\", \")\n    : String(rawValue ?? \"\").trim();\n\n  const operator = String(filter.operator || \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n\n  if (\n    attributeName === \"exception\" &&\n    attributeValue.toLowerCase() === \"none\" &&\n    [\"not equals\", \"not equal\", \"!=\", \"<>\"].includes(operator)\n  ) {\n    return \"exists\";\n  }\n\n  if (\n    attributeName === \"exception\" &&\n    attributeValue.toLowerCase() === \"none\" &&\n    [\"equals\", \"equal\", \"=\"].includes(operator)\n  ) {\n    return \"does not exist\";\n  }\n\n  if (rawValue === null && [\"not equals\", \"not equal\", \"!=\", \"<>\"].includes(operator)) {\n    return \"exists\";\n  }\n\n  if (rawValue === null && [\"equals\", \"equal\", \"=\"].includes(operator)) {\n    return \"does not exist\";\n  }\n\n  if (!operator) {\n    return attributeValue;\n  }\n\n  if (operator === \"in\") {\n    return `in ${attributeValue}`;\n  }\n\n  const dateAttributes = new Set([\n    \"creationDate\",\n    \"dueDate\",\n    \"invoiceDate\",\n    \"timeCreated\"\n  ]);\n\n  const dateOperatorLabels = {\n    \"greater than or equal to\": \"on or after\",\n    \"less than or equal to\": \"on or before\",\n    \"greater than\": \"after\",\n    \"less than\": \"before\",\n    \"not equals\": \"not equal to\",\n    \"equals\": \"\"\n  };\n\n  const genericOperatorLabels = {\n    \"greater than or equal to\": \"greater than or equal to\",\n    \"less than or equal to\": \"less than or equal to\",\n    \"greater than\": \"greater than\",\n    \"less than\": \"less than\",\n    \"not equals\": \"not equal to\",\n    \"equals\": \"\"\n  };\n\n  const operatorLabels = dateAttributes.has(attributeName)\n    ? dateOperatorLabels\n    : genericOperatorLabels;\n\n  const label = operatorLabels[operator] ?? operator;\n\n  return label ? `${label} ${attributeValue}` : attributeValue;\n}\n\nfunction getDisplayValue(filter) {\n  const displayValue = String(filter.displayValue || \"\").trim();\n\n  if (displayValue) {\n    return displayValue;\n  }\n\n  return formatCriteriaValue(filter);\n}\n\nfunction buildCriteriaRows(filters) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(filters)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  return filters\n    .map((filter, index) => {\n      if (!filter || !filter.attributeName) {\n        return null;\n      }\n\n      const override = getDisplayOverride(filter);\n\n      if (override) {\n        return {\n          rowId: `criteria-${index + 1}`,\n          ...override\n        };\n      }\n\n      const parameter = getCriteriaLabel(String(filter.attributeName || \"\").trim());\n      const value = getDisplayValue(filter);\n\n      if (!parameter || !value) {\n        return null;\n      }\n\n      return {\n        rowId: `criteria-${index + 1}`,\n        Parameter: parameter,\n        Value: value\n      };\n    })\n    .filter(Boolean);\n}\n\nfunction buildCriteriaTable(filters) {\n  const rows = buildCriteriaRows(filters);\n\n  if (rows.length === 0) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  return {\n    display_type: \"table\",\n    display_sequence: 3,\n    rows: {\n      items: rows\n    },\n    columns: {\n      items: [\n        {\n          headerText: \"Parameter\",\n          field: \"Parameter\",\n          id: \"Parameter\",\n          resizable: \"enabled\",\n          className: \"\",\n          template: \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          headerText: \"Value\",\n          field: \"Value\",\n          id: \"Value\",\n          resizable: \"enabled\",\n          className: \"\",\n          template: \"\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    keyAttributes: {\n      items: [\"rowId\"]\n    },\n    accessibility: {\n      \"row.accessible-row-header\": \"Parameter\"\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nconst criteriaTable = buildCriteriaTable(extractedFilters);\n\nconst agentResponse = [\n  {\n    display_type: \"text\",\n    display_sequence: 1,\n    text: responseText\n  },\n  {\n    display_type: \"canvas\",\n    display_sequence: 2,\n    canvas_content: {\n      filters: extractedFilters,\n      serviceFilter,\n      serviceEndpoint\n    }\n  }\n];\n\nif (criteriaTable) {\n  agentResponse.push(criteriaTable);\n}\n\nreturn {\n  agent_response: agentResponse\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_RETURN_FILTER_VALID",
          "id": "1777618997874",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Route Insight Flow"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1781074919894",
            "false": "1780294546466"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_ROUTE_INSIGHT_FLOW",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1777618768205",
          "id": "1781074638109",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781074638110_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.FLOWINSIGHTNAME != null && $context.$triggers.REST.$input.FLOWINSIGHTNAME.trim() != ''}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Route Attribute Extraction"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "standardInvoices": "1780295814511",
            "rejectedInvoices": "1780295848841",
            "unsupportedInquiry": "1780489721020"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_ROUTE_ATTRIBUTE_EXTRACTION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1777618768205",
          "id": "1780295778205",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780295778206_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_ROUTE_INVOICE_REQUEST.$output.route}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Extract Attributes Standard Invoice"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780298075966"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_EXTRACT_ATTRIBUTES_STANDARD_INVOICE",
          "id": "1780295814511",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780295814513_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a standard invoice filter extraction engine.\n\nExtract only the filters or criteria explicitly mentioned in the actual user message.\n\nActual user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nCurrent date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nCurrent date-time:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nReturn only a valid JSON array.\nDo not return SQL, explanations, or markdown.\nDo not include filters from examples.\nDo not infer missing filters.\n\nSupported attributes:\ninvoiceId\nstreamDetailId\ndocumentName\nstreamCode\nstream\ninvoiceNumber\nsupplierName\ninvoiceAmount\ndueDate\nbusinessUnit\nsupplierSite\npurchaseOrderNumber\ncreationDate\nstatus\nstatusCode\napprovalStatusCode\napprovalStatus\npaidStatusCode\npaidStatus\ninvoiceStatusCode\ninvoiceStatus\ntype\nsource\ncurrencyCode\nexceptionCode\nexception\naccountCodingStatus\naccountCodingStatusCode\nfundsStatus\nfundsStatusCode\n\nComparison attributes:\ndueDate\ncreationDate\ninvoiceAmount\n\nSupported operators:\nequals\nnot equals\ngreater than\nless than\ngreater than or equal to\nless than or equal to\n\nMapping rules:\n- Invoice ID maps to invoiceId.\n- Invoice number maps to invoiceNumber.\n- Supplier maps to supplierName.\n- Business unit maps to businessUnit.\n- Supplier site maps to supplierSite.\n- Purchase order, PO, or PO number maps to purchaseOrderNumber.\n- Invoice amount maps to invoiceAmount.\n- Due date maps to dueDate.\n- Created date, creation date, created time, or creation time maps to creationDate.\n- Type or invoice type maps to type.\n- Source maps to source.\n- Currency maps to currencyCode.\n- Validation status maps to status.\n- Validation status code maps to statusCode.\n- Invoice status maps to invoiceStatus.\n- Invoice status code maps to invoiceStatusCode.\n- Approval status or workflow approval status maps to approvalStatus.\n- Approval status code maps to approvalStatusCode.\n- Paid status or payment status maps to paidStatus.\n- Paid status code or payment status code maps to paidStatusCode.\n- Exception maps to exception.\n- Exception code maps to exceptionCode.\n- Account coding status maps to accountCodingStatus.\n- Account coding status code maps to accountCodingStatusCode.\n- Funds status maps to fundsStatus.\n- Fund status maps to fundsStatus.\n- Funds status code maps to fundsStatusCode.\n- Fund status code maps to fundsStatusCode.\n- If the user says only \"status\", use status.\n- If the user says only \"code\", use the code attribute for the nearby concept.\n- If the user says \"policy violations\" or \"policy violation\" without explicitly saying invoice status, map it to exception with value \"Policy Violations\".\n- If the user explicitly says invoice status policy violations, map it to invoiceStatus with value \"Policy Violations\".\n- If the user says policy violation type, map the provided policy violation type value to exception.\n\nRules:\n- Use only supported attributes.\n- Every output object must include attributeName and attributeValue.\n- Do not output a filter if no attributeValue can be determined, except for null-check filters.\n- If the user mentions only an invoice number, return only invoiceNumber.\n- Do not extract rejected status in this prompt.\n- Do not output stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode or timeCreated.\n- For comparison attributes, include an operator.\n- If a comparison attribute is mentioned without a comparison, use \"equals\".\n- invoiceAmount must contain only the numeric value.\n- If amount and currency are mentioned together, split them into invoiceAmount and currencyCode.\n- If an attribute is mentioned but no usable value is provided, do not output a filter for that attribute.\n- Values may be provided inside braces, such as Supplier {SUPPLIER_VALUE}; use the trimmed text inside the braces as the value.\n- Empty braces such as Supplier {}, whitespace-only values, blank text, or missing values are not usable values.\n- Currency codes must be uppercase.\n- For exception value \"none\", output \"None\".\n- If the user says \"pending approval\", output approvalStatusCode with attributeValue [\"INITIATED\",\"REQUIRED\",\"STOPPED\",\"REJECTED\",\"NEEDS WFREAPPROVAL\",\"SUSPENDED\"] and the operator as 'IN'.\n- When a user-facing status value is expanded into backend status codes, include displayValue with the original user-facing value.\n- The backend codes must remain in attributeValue.\n- displayValue is only for user-facing response display.\n\nExistence rules:\n- If the user says an attribute exists, existing, is present, is available, has a value, or is not null, output that attribute with attributeValue null and operator \"not equals\".\n- If the user says an attribute is missing, does not exist, is blank, is empty, has no value, or is null, output that attribute with attributeValue null and operator \"equals\".\n- For null-check filters, include attributeValue as JSON null, not the string \"null\".\n- Exception is special: if the user asks for invoices where exception exists, has exceptions, or has an exception, output exception with attributeValue \"None\" and operator \"not equals\".\n- Exception is special: if the user asks for invoices where exception is missing, has no exception, or has no exceptions, output exception with attributeValue \"None\" and operator \"equals\".\n\nDate rules:\n- dueDate must be date-only.\n- creationDate is a date-time field, but extraction must output date-only values for whole-day or period requests.\n- \"created today\", \"created yesterday\", or \"created on a specific date\" means creationDate with date only and operator \"equals\".\n- \"created after today\" means creationDate with current date-time plus Z and operator \"greater than\".\n- \"created before today\" means creationDate with current date-time plus Z and operator \"less than\".\n- \"due today\" means dueDate with current date and operator \"equals\".\n- \"due on or before today\" means dueDate with current date and operator \"less than or equal to\".\n- \"due after today\" means dueDate with current date and operator \"greater than\".\n- \"overdue invoices\" means dueDate with current date and operator \"less than\".\n- Specific day dates may be written with month names or abbreviations, ordinal day suffixes, or without a year.\n- Ignore ordinal suffixes when parsing specific day dates.\n- If a specific day date has no year, use the current year.\n- If the user gives \"Invoice Creation Date From DATE\" without a to/end date, output one creationDate filter with operator \"greater than or equal to\".\n- If the user gives \"Invoice Creation Date To DATE\" without a from/start date, output one creationDate filter with operator \"less than or equal to\".\n- If the user asks for invoices created in, created during, created for, creation date in, or from a specific year, treat it as a full-year creationDate range.\n- If the user asks for invoices created in, created during, created for, creation date in, or from a specific month, treat it as a full-month creationDate range.\n- If the month request has no year, use the current year.\n- For full-year creationDate ranges, output two creationDate filters: one with operator \"greater than or equal to\" using the first day of the year, and one with operator \"less than or equal to\" using the last day of the year.\n- For full-month creationDate ranges, output two creationDate filters: one with operator \"greater than or equal to\" using the first day of the month, and one with operator \"less than or equal to\" using the last day of the month.\n- If the user asks for invoices due in, due during, due for, due date in, or due from a specific year, treat it as a full-year dueDate range.\n- If the user asks for invoices due in, due during, due for, due date in, or due from a specific month, treat it as a full-month dueDate range.\n- For full-year dueDate ranges, output two dueDate filters: one with operator \"greater than or equal to\" using the first day of the year, and one with operator \"less than or equal to\" using the last day of the year.\n- For full-month dueDate ranges, output two dueDate filters: one with operator \"greater than or equal to\" using the first day of the month, and one with operator \"less than or equal to\" using the last day of the month.\n- Never output a year-only value as attributeValue for creationDate or dueDate.\n- Never output a month-only value as attributeValue for creationDate or dueDate.\n- Never output a month-and-year phrase as attributeValue for creationDate or dueDate.\n- Date attributeValue must be either YYYY-MM-DD, a date-time value only where explicitly required, or a calculated YYYY-MM-DD boundary for a range.\n- Do not infer a date attribute from an unqualified month or year unless the user clearly connects it to created, creation date, due, or due date.\n\nPending age rules:\n- If the user says pending for greater than N days, pending more than N days, pending over N days, days pending greater than N, or days pending from invoice creation date, map it to creationDate.\n- Pending day values may be numeric or written in words.\n- Convert written day values to numbers before calculating the pending-age date.\n- For pending greater than N days, output creationDate with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"less than\".\n- For pending greater than or equal to N days, output creationDate with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"less than or equal to\".\n- If the user says pending for less than N days, pending less than N days, pending under N days, pending below N days, or days pending less than N, map it to creationDate.\n- For pending less than N days, output creationDate with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"greater than\".\n- For pending less than or equal to N days, output creationDate with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"greater than or equal to\".\n- Approval pending status and pending age are separate filters. If the prompt contains both pending approval and pending less/greater than N days, output both approvalStatusCode and creationDate filters.\n- If the user includes both an explicit creation date range and a pending-days filter, output both filters.\n\nExamples:\n\nIn examples, placeholder values written as PLACEHOLDER_VALUE are examples only.\nWhen processing the actual user message, replace placeholders with the exact value from the actual user message.\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices pending for greater than DAYS_VALUE days\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"creationDate\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"CURRENT_DATE_MINUS_DAYS_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"less than\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoice with invoice number INVOICE_NUMBER_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_NUMBER_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoice with invoice ID INVOICE_ID_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceId\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_ID_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices from supplier SUPPLIER_NAME_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"supplierName\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"SUPPLIER_NAME_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices for business unit BUSINESS_UNIT_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"businessUnit\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"BUSINESS_UNIT_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices with supplier site SUPPLIER_SITE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"supplierSite\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"SUPPLIER_SITE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices for PO PO_NUMBER_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"PO_NUMBER_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices with PO number existing\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": null,\n    \"operator\": \"not equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices with PO number missing\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": null,\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices with amount greater than AMOUNT_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceAmount\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"AMOUNT_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"greater than\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices with amount greater than AMOUNT_VALUE CURRENCY_CODE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceAmount\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"AMOUNT_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"greater than\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"currencyCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"CURRENCY_CODE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices in currency CURRENCY_CODE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"currencyCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"CURRENCY_CODE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nList invoices with validation status STATUS_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"status\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"STATUS_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nList invoices with validation status code STATUS_CODE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"statusCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"STATUS_CODE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nList invoices with invoice status INVOICE_STATUS_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceStatus\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_STATUS_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nList invoices with invoice status code INVOICE_STATUS_CODE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceStatusCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_STATUS_CODE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with approval status APPROVAL_STATUS_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"approvalStatus\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"APPROVAL_STATUS_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with payment status PAID_STATUS_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"paidStatus\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"PAID_STATUS_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with exception EXCEPTION_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"exception\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"EXCEPTION_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with exceptions\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"exception\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"None\",\n    \"operator\": \"not equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with no exceptions\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"exception\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"None\",\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with type TYPE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"type\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"TYPE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow invoices with source SOURCE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"source\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"SOURCE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices created today\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"creationDate\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\",\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me invoices due on or before today\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"dueDate\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\",\n    \"operator\": \"less than or equal to\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me overdue invoices\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"dueDate\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\",\n    \"operator\": \"less than\"\n  }\n]\n\nNow extract filters from the actual user message only.\nReturn only the JSON array."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
