            },
            "name": "Extract Attributes Rejected Invoice"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780298106606"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_EXTRACT_ATTRIBUTES_REJECTED_INVOICE",
          "id": "1780295848841",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780295848842_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a staged invoice filter extraction engine.\n\nExtract only the filters or criteria explicitly mentioned in the actual user message.\n\nThis prompt is only for staged/rejected invoice searches.\nUse only the supported staged invoice attributes listed below.\n\nActual user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nCurrent date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nCurrent date-time:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nReturn only a valid JSON array.\nDo not return SQL, explanations, or markdown.\nDo not include filters from examples.\nDo not infer missing filters.\n\nSupported staged invoice attributes:\ninvoiceId\ndocumentStreamDetail.streamDetailId\ndocumentStreamDetail.name\ndocumentStreamDetail.stream.lookupCode\ndocumentStreamDetail.stream.meaning\ninvoiceNumber\nsupplier.name\ninvoiceAmount\nbusinessUnit.name\nsupplierSite.name\npurchaseOrderNumber\ntimeCreated\nstagedInvoiceStatus.meaning\nstagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\ninvoiceStatus.lookupCode\ninvoiceStatus.meaning\ninvoiceTypeCode.meaning\ninvoiceSource.meaning\ninvoiceCurrency.currencyCode\nexception.lookupCode\nexception.meaning\n\nComparison attributes:\ninvoiceAmount\ntimeCreated\n\nSupported operators:\nequals\nnot equals\ngreater than\nless than\ngreater than or equal to\nless than or equal to\n\nMapping rules:\n- Invoice ID maps to invoiceId.\n- Invoice number maps to invoiceNumber.\n- Supplier maps to supplier.name.\n- Business unit maps to businessUnit.name.\n- Supplier site maps to supplierSite.name.\n- Purchase order, PO, or PO number maps to purchaseOrderNumber.\n- Invoice amount maps to invoiceAmount.\n- Created date, creation date, created time, or creation time maps to timeCreated.\n- Document stream detail ID or stream detail ID maps to documentStreamDetail.streamDetailId.\n- Document name maps to documentStreamDetail.name.\n- Stream code maps to documentStreamDetail.stream.lookupCode.\n- Stream maps to documentStreamDetail.stream.meaning.\n- Status maps to stagedInvoiceStatus.meaning.\n- Status code maps to stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode.\n- Rejected status maps to stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode with value REJECTED.\n- Invoice status maps to invoiceStatus.meaning.\n- Invoice status code maps to invoiceStatus.lookupCode.\n- Type or invoice type maps to invoiceTypeCode.meaning.\n- Source maps to invoiceSource.meaning.\n- Currency maps to invoiceCurrency.currencyCode.\n- Exception maps to exception.meaning.\n- Exception code maps to exception.lookupCode.\n- If the user says only \"status\", use stagedInvoiceStatus.meaning.\n- If the user says only \"code\", use the code attribute for the nearby concept.\n\nRules:\n- Always include stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode = REJECTED for rejected invoice requests.\n- Use only supported staged invoice attributes.\n- Every output object must include attributeName and attributeValue.\n- Do not output a filter if no attributeValue can be determined, except for null-check filters.\n- For comparison attributes, include an operator.\n- If a comparison attribute is mentioned without a comparison, use \"equals\".\n- invoiceAmount must contain only the numeric value.\n- If amount and currency are mentioned together, split them into invoiceAmount and invoiceCurrency.currencyCode.\n- If an attribute is mentioned but no usable value is provided, do not output a filter for that attribute.\n- Values may be provided inside braces, such as Supplier {SUPPLIER_VALUE}; use the trimmed text inside the braces as the value.\n- Empty braces such as Supplier {}, whitespace-only values, blank text, or missing values are not usable values.\n- Currency codes must be uppercase.\n- If the user mentions policy violation or policy violations, output exception.meaning with attributeValue exactly \"Policy Violations\", unless the user explicitly says invoice status.\n- For exception value \"none\", output \"None\".\n- When a user-facing status value is expanded into backend status codes, include displayValue with the original user-facing value.\n- The backend codes must remain in attributeValue.\n- displayValue is only for user-facing response display.\n\nExistence rules:\n- If the user says an attribute exists, existing, is present, is available, has a value, or is not null, output that attribute with attributeValue null and operator \"not equals\".\n- If the user says an attribute is missing, does not exist, is blank, is empty, has no value, or is null, output that attribute with attributeValue null and operator \"equals\".\n- For null-check filters, include attributeValue as JSON null, not the string \"null\".\n- Exception is special: if the user asks for invoices where exception exists, has exceptions, or has an exception, output exception.meaning with attributeValue \"None\" and operator \"not equals\".\n- Exception is special: if the user asks for invoices where exception is missing, has no exception, or has no exceptions, output exception.meaning with attributeValue \"None\" and operator \"equals\".\n\nDate rules:\n- timeCreated is a date-time field, but extraction must output date-only values for whole-day or period requests.\n- \"created today\", \"created yesterday\", or \"created on a specific date\" means timeCreated with date only and operator \"equals\".\n- \"created after today\" means timeCreated with current date-time plus Z and operator \"greater than\".\n- \"created before today\" means timeCreated with current date-time plus Z and operator \"less than\".\n- \"created on or after today\" means timeCreated with current date only and operator \"greater than or equal to\".\n- \"created on or before today\" means timeCreated with current date only and operator \"less than or equal to\".\n- Specific day dates may be written with month names or abbreviations, ordinal day suffixes, or without a year.\n- Ignore ordinal suffixes when parsing specific day dates.\n- If a specific day date has no year, use the current year.\n- If the user gives \"Invoice Creation Date From DATE\" or \"Created From DATE\" without a to/end date, output one timeCreated filter with operator \"greater than or equal to\".\n- If the user gives \"Invoice Creation Date To DATE\" or \"Created To DATE\" without a from/start date, output one timeCreated filter with operator \"less than or equal to\".\n- If the user asks for rejected invoices created in, created during, created for, creation date in, or from a specific year, treat it as a full-year timeCreated range.\n- If the user asks for rejected invoices created in, created during, created for, creation date in, or from a specific month, treat it as a full-month timeCreated range.\n- If the month request has no year, use the current year.\n- For full-year timeCreated ranges, output stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode with value REJECTED, plus two timeCreated filters: one with operator \"greater than or equal to\" using the first day of the year, and one with operator \"less than or equal to\" using the last day of the year.\n- For full-month timeCreated ranges, output stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode with value REJECTED, plus two timeCreated filters: one with operator \"greater than or equal to\" using the first day of the month, and one with operator \"less than or equal to\" using the last day of the month.\n- Never output a year-only value as attributeValue for timeCreated.\n- Never output a month-only value as attributeValue for timeCreated.\n- Never output a month-and-year phrase as attributeValue for timeCreated.\n- timeCreated attributeValue must be either YYYY-MM-DD, a date-time value only where explicitly required, or a calculated YYYY-MM-DD boundary for a range.\n- Do not infer a date attribute from an unqualified month or year unless the user clearly connects it to created or creation date.\n\nPending age rules:\n- If the user says pending for greater than N days, pending more than N days, pending over N days, days pending greater than N, or days pending from invoice creation date, map it to timeCreated.\n- Pending day values may be numeric or written in words.\n- Convert written day values to numbers before calculating the pending-age date.\n- For pending greater than N days, output timeCreated with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"less than\".\n- For pending greater than or equal to N days, output timeCreated with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"less than or equal to\".\n- If the user says pending for less than N days, pending less than N days, pending under N days, pending below N days, or days pending less than N, map it to creationDate.\n- For pending less than N days, output creationDate with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"greater than\".\n- For pending less than or equal to N days, output creationDate with value equal to current date minus N days in YYYY-MM-DD format and operator \"greater than or equal to\".\n- Approval pending status and pending age are separate filters. If the prompt contains both pending approval and pending less/greater than N days, output both approvalStatusCode and creationDate filters.\n- If the user includes both an explicit created date range and a pending-days filter, output both filters.\n\nExamples:\n\nIn examples, placeholder values written as PLACEHOLDER_VALUE are examples only.\nWhen processing the actual user message, replace placeholders with the exact value from the actual user message.\n\nUser message:\nShow rejected invoices pending for greater than DAYS_VALUE days\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"timeCreated\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"CURRENT_DATE_MINUS_DAYS_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"less than\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoice with invoice number INVOICE_NUMBER_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_NUMBER_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoice with invoice ID INVOICE_ID_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceId\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"INVOICE_ID_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices from supplier SUPPLIER_NAME_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"supplier.name\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"SUPPLIER_NAME_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices for business unit BUSINESS_UNIT_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"businessUnit.name\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"BUSINESS_UNIT_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with supplier site SUPPLIER_SITE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"supplierSite.name\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"SUPPLIER_SITE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices for PO PO_NUMBER_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"PO_NUMBER_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with PO number existing\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": null,\n    \"operator\": \"not equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with PO number missing\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n    \"attributeValue\": null,\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with amount greater than AMOUNT_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceAmount\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"AMOUNT_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"greater than\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with amount greater than AMOUNT_VALUE CURRENCY_CODE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceAmount\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"AMOUNT_VALUE\",\n    \"operator\": \"greater than\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceCurrency.currencyCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"CURRENCY_CODE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with exceptions\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"exception.meaning\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"None\",\n    \"operator\": \"not equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with no exceptions\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"exception.meaning\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"None\",\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with type TYPE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceTypeCode.meaning\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"TYPE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices with source SOURCE_VALUE\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"invoiceSource.meaning\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"SOURCE_VALUE\"\n  }\n]\n\nUser message:\nShow me rejected invoices created today\n\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"stagedInvoiceStatus.lookupCode\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"REJECTED\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"attributeName\": \"timeCreated\",\n    \"attributeValue\": \"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\",\n    \"operator\": \"equals\"\n  }\n]\n\nNow extract filters from the actual user message only.\nReturn only the JSON array."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Filter Rejected Invoice"
